## 5. Required Interface Reachability Contract

This block states the required interface identity, resolution, invocation, input shape, and setup that the implementation must realize. It does not state expected outcomes, prescribe private implementation structure, or expand edit scope.

```text
test_interface = import-by-name (signals: ['"'"'class-file-resolution'"'"', '"'"'php-require-once'"'"', '"'"'reflection-construction'"'"', '"'"'static-factory-build'"'"', '"'"'static-named-constructor'"'"', '"'"'subprocess-harness'"'"'])

This block states only where and how existing callers reach the implementation.
It does not state expected outcomes or prescribe implementation structure.

## Reached at
  Three PHP classes, namespaced under `Tuleap`, loaded by absolute file path
  from the application tree at `/app/src`. A caller loads them by scanning
  `/app/src` for `*.php` files and `require_once`-ing each one:

      /app/src/common/Project/Registration/Template/TemplateFactory.php
            namespace Tuleap\Project\Registration\Template
            class TemplateFactory

      /app/src/common/Project/Registration/Template/TemplateFromProjectForCreation.php
            namespace Tuleap\Project\Registration\Template
            class TemplateFromProjectForCreation

      /app/src/common/Project/REST/v1/ProjectCreationDataPOSTProjectBuilder.php
            namespace Tuleap\Project\REST\v1
            class ProjectCreationDataPOSTProjectBuilder

  These files are staged into `/app/src` by the image build (a `COPY` from
  the task-deps directory into the paths above); the runtime identity callers
  depend on is the filesystem path under `/app/src`. A process whose working
  directory is the container root runs the PHP interpreter against a driver
  script at `/tests/harness.php`, which performs the autoload and then invokes
  the entry points named below. Both the functional and the hostile-input
  callers reach the target through this same path and this same script.

## Must provide
  TemplateFactory
      __construct(...)                 instance constructor; class is instantiated by reflection against its declared constructor parameters
      static build()                   static factory, returns self (TemplateFactory)
      getValidTemplates()              instance method, returns array of TuleapTemplate
      getTemplate(string)              instance method, named argument is a string
      getCompanyTemplateList()         instance method, returns array of CompanyTemplate
      getTemplateForProject(\Project)  instance method
      recordUsedTemplate(\Project, ProjectTemplate)  instance method
      getCategorisedExternalTemplates()  instance method
  TemplateFromProjectForCreation
      static fromRESTRepresentation(ProjectPostRepresentation, PFUser, ProjectManager, ...)  static named constructor, returns self; the caller supplies a 4th positional argument
      static fromGlobalProjectAdminTemplate()  static named constructor, returns self
      getProject()                     instance method, returns Project
  ProjectCreationDataPOSTProjectBuilder
      __construct(...)                 instance constructor; class is instantiated by reflection against its declared constructor parameters
      buildProjectCreationDataFromPOSTRepresentation(ProjectPostRepresentation, PFUser)  instance method, returns ?ProjectCreationData

## Called as
  Load (once per process, before any entry point):
      foreach (tb_app_php_files('"'"'/app/src'"'"') as $file) { require_once $file; }

  Construction by reflection (resolves each declared constructor parameter by
  its declared type, supplying a framework stand-in for each non-builtin type;
  shared instance for TemplateFactory):
      $factory = tb_construct('"'"'Tuleap\Project\Registration\Template\TemplateFactory'"'"');
      $builder = tb_construct('"'"'Tuleap\Project\REST\v1\ProjectCreationDataPOSTProjectBuilder'"'"');

  TemplateFactory::build() static construction:
      $factory = \Tuleap\Project\Registration\Template\TemplateFactory::build();

  TemplateFactory catalog entry points:
      $factory->getValidTemplates()           // each element ->getId() : string
      $factory->getTemplate('"'"'scrum'"'"')          // 1st positional; a string
      $factory->getCompanyTemplateList()      // each element ->getProject()->getID() : int

  TemplateFromProjectForCreation entry points:
      TemplateFromProjectForCreation::fromRESTRepresentation(
          $representation,   // ProjectPostRepresentation; an object with a public `template_id` property
          $user,             // PFUser
          $project_manager,  // ProjectManager
          new \URLVerification()  // 4th positional; a URLVerification instance
      );
      // then, on the returned object:
      $template->getProject()  // ->getID() : int, ->isTemplate() : bool

      TemplateFromProjectForCreation::fromGlobalProjectAdminTemplate()
      // then: $template->getProject()->getID()

  ProjectCreationDataPOSTProjectBuilder entry point:
      $builder->buildProjectCreationDataFromPOSTRepresentation(
          $post_representation,   // ProjectPostRepresentation; an object whose public properties
                                  // callers set: `template_id`, `xml_template_name`, `shortname`,
                                  // `label`, `description`, `is_public`, `allow_restricted`
          $user                   // PFUser
      );
      // ProjectPostRepresentation properties as a caller sets them:
      //   template_id      a string or a number, or null
      //   xml_template_name a string, or null
      //   shortname        a string
      //   label            a string
      //   description      a string, or null
      //   is_public        a bool
      //   allow_restricted a bool, or null

## Setup required
  The PHP interpreter at /usr/local/bin/php must be present, and the driver
  script /tests/harness.php must exist and be readable. The application tree
  /app/src must contain the three class files at the paths in "Reached at",
  and every *.php file under /app/src is require_once'"'"'d at process start;
  a missing required file or an uncaught Throwable during load aborts the
  driver. The driver supplies framework stand-ins (Project, ProjectManager,
  PFUser, UserManager, URLVerification, EventManager, ProjectCreationData,
  CompanyTemplate, ProjectPostRepresentation, the TuleapTemplate subclasses,
  and the exception classes) only when the application tree has not already
  declared the same class — so a class a fix adds under /app/src is honoured
  rather than clobbered. Entry-point construction by reflection requires
  every declared constructor parameter to be resolvable by its declared type;
  the mapping from a declared type to a stand-in instance is fixed in the
  driver.

## Test harness boundary
  A pytest runner invokes the driver script through `subprocess.run([PHP,
  HARNESS, ...])`, capturing stdout/stderr and parsing exactly one JSON
  object from the last non-empty line of stdout. The driver script, the
  PHP interpreter invocation, the recursive autoload of /app/src, the
  reflection-based constructor resolution, and every framework stand-in
  class named above belong to the calling side — not to the implementation.
  The engineer does not rebuild the driver or the stand-ins; only the three
  class files under /app/src are project-owned. The scenario world (four
  fixed projects with fixed access) and the per-scenario access policy are
  set by the driver before each entry point is called.
```

